  "marker_transfer": "For a compatible Gaussian source charge grading with absolute variable charges<=w,a jointly pure pairS,T of charges-1,+1,and a fixed markerQ0 with L[Q0 S^i T^j]=delta_ij*a_i for a nonzero rational normalized prime-separating sequence,ALL zero-constantH(S,T) are classified:full safety iff every occurring i-j has one strict sign. The marked Laurent embedding s=z,t=r/z is injective and PSMT1 gives necessity;source charge separation gives cutoffm*eta>wdegQ for all markers. This is a reusable certificate theorem,not a general Gaussian support classifier.",
  "complete_classification": "For the known six-variable pair,Q0=1+xy has radial momentsa_n=(2n)!/2^n from its square-root periodU. Direct factorial-ratio products prove normalized prime separation for every odd prime. Hence EVERY individualH(S,T) is safe exactly when its collected charge support is strictly one-sided;the zero phase is separate. All otherH are pure-null failures with the SAME fixed quadratic markerxy and a nonzero k*p subsequence for all sufficiently large primes. Common field slope2 is sharp across the entire algebra and all recomposition degrees;individual sufficient slope is2/min|i-j|. This closes the previously open mixed-charge classification for this explicit pair,not all cotangent algebras.",
  "safe_scheme": "At recomposition degree<=d,the reduced safe coefficient scheme is the union of the positive/negative charge coordinate spaces. Its explicit radical monomial ideal isJ=(neutral coefficients,products c_positive*c_negative). Over every coefficient K-algebra safety is exactly nilpotence ofJA. If(JA)^L=0,a direct charge/pairing argument gives affine cutoffm>2degQ+(d+1)(L-1),hence common integer slopeC_L=2+(d+1)(L-1). Full ordinary cutoff ideals satisfyI_(C_L) subsetJ^L and radical(I_N)=J forN>=2;their filtrations are cofinal. No equality of individual cutoff levels withJ or its powers is claimed. Disconnected reduced algebras may choose different signs on components.",
  "normalization": "For the entire pure coefficient family,the exact polynomial-Hom normalization ideal isGamma_J(A)=union_k Ann_A((JA)^k). Its universal relative Hom is0,while every fiber on either positive-dimensional safe coordinate subspace has Hom dimension1. This strengthens the earlier origin-only pure-family base-change control;it does not refute valid fiberwise methods. LiteralJA0 is sufficient but not necessary at nonreduced safe points,and the normalization ideal is not an ordinary moment cutoff ideal.",
  "implementation": "An exact Q(i)[s,t] classifier now decides ALL degrees for this fixed algebra by collected charge support,returning a positive cutoff or the fixed quadratic bad marker. A guarded marked coefficient extractor and small explicit safe-ideal generator are implemented. Tests include a balanced polynomial with its first quadratic marked moment0 but its next one1656,so the classifier is not a prefix heuristic. No large prime/grid campaign,general Gaussian classifier,ordinary cutoff/Hom solver or high inverse expansion is used.",
